# A machine-generated dump: a diff of it is never read, and the change that
# matters is already in the commit message.
flake.lock -diff

# SOPS ciphertext. `-text` keeps git from touching its line endings, which would
# corrupt it, and `-diff` stops one re-encryption from reading as a whole-file
# change. `sops -d` and `just secrets-update` are how these are reviewed.
secrets/** -text -diff

# Icons are read by macOS, never by a person.
*.icns binary
